## SVG Label Update Process

### Text Replacement Strategy
1. **Load Base SVG**: Fetch SVG content from database or local assets
2. **Remove Existing Text**: Strip all `<text>` elements from SVG
3. **Inject New Labels**: Replace text elements with current measurement values
4. **Regex Replacement**: Use field labels to find and replace specific text elements

```typescript
// Example text replacement
manualFields.forEach((field) => {
  const value = measurements[field.field_name] || 0;
  const fieldLabel = field.field_label;
  const labelRegex = new RegExp(`(<text[^>]*>\\s*<tspan[^>]*>\\s*)${fieldLabel.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&')}(\\s*</tspan>\\s*</text>)`, 'g');
  completeSvg = completeSvg.replace(labelRegex, (match, startTag, endTag) => {
    return `${startTag}${fieldLabel}: ${value.toFixed(3)} in${endTag}`;
  });
});
```

## Wall Toggle System
- **Per-Field Toggles**: Each measurement field has a wall toggle
- **Edge Calculation**: Only non-wall measurements contribute to edge pricing
- **Visual Feedback**: Toggle state visually indicates wall contact

## Backsplash System
- **Global Toggle**: Single toggle for entire shape
- **Height Input**: Configurable backsplash height (1-24 inches)
- **Area Calculation**: Perimeter × height added to total area
- **Pricing**: Included in material cost calculation

## Unit System
- **Input Units**: All measurements input in inches
- **Internal Calculations**: Convert to feet for area calculations
- **Display Units**: Show "in" labels throughout interface
- **Conversion Factor**: 1 foot = 12 inches
